test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:25:29:
   |
25 | unknown :: Files[each #p in nope] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                             ^
unknown name nope; name a value with #nope in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:27:37:
   |
27 | notList Path#ps :: Files[each #p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                     ^
ps is a Path, not a list, so each #p in ps can't pick elements of Files

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:29:39:
   |
29 | wrongKey Names#ps :: Files[each #p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                       ^
ps holds BranchName, but the key of Files is Path

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:31:41:
   |
31 | listOfLists Nest#ps :: Files[each #p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                         ^
ps holds Paths, but the key of Files is Path

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:33:51:
   |
33 | named OneAndAll(Path#p * Paths#ps) :: Files[each #p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                                   ^
p is named twice in this transition

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:36:48:
   |
36 |   :: App(Files[each #p in ps] * Branches[each #b in bs]) -> App(Files[p] * Branches[b])
   |                                                ^
a transition picks several elements once; Files[each #p in ps] already does here

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:38:45:
   |
38 | targetOnly Paths#ps :: Files -> Files[each #p in ps](FileState.Conflicted)
   |                                             ^
on the target side, write Files[p]; each #p names the key on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:41:64:
   |
41 |   :: Files[each #p in ps](FileState.Unmodified) -> Files[each #p in ps](FileState.Conflicted)
   |                                                                ^
on the target side, write Files[p]; each #p names the key on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:43:53:
   |
43 | inGuard Paths#ps :: App => Mode.Idle // Files[each #p in ps](FileState.Conflicted) -> Mode.Busy
   |                                                     ^
a guard can't pick elements with Files[each #p in ps]; write it on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:45:21:
   |
45 | unkeyed Paths#ps :: Plain[each #p in ps] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                     ^
Plain has no key, so [each #p in ps] can't pick elements; declare one, such as Plain = [FileState by Path]

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:47:33:
   |
47 | unnamedUnknown :: Files[each in nope] => FileState.Unmodified -> FileState.Conflicted
   |                                 ^
unknown name nope; name a value with #nope in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:49:42:
   |
49 | unnamedTarget Paths#ps :: Files -> Files[each in ps](FileState.Conflicted)
   |                                          ^
on the target side, Files[each in ps] can't be written; name the key on the source side, Files[each #p in ps], and write Files[p] here

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:51:52:
   |
51 | unnamedGuard Paths#ps :: App => Mode.Idle // Files[each in ps](FileState.Conflicted) -> Mode.Busy
   |                                                    ^
a guard can't pick elements with Files[each in ps]; write it on the source side

test/check/error-element-in.sumspec:53:73:
   |
53 | unnamedUse Paths#ps :: Files[each in ps](FileState.Unmodified) -> Files[p](FileState.Conflicted)
   |                                                                         ^
unknown name p; name a value with #p in the input or on the source side

